  - nodeId: wh_dublin
    lines:
    - speakerId: narrator
      language: 0
      text: "29 listopada 2010. Wczoraj Irlandia przyj\u0119\u0142a pomoc Unii Europejskiej i Mi\u0119dzynarodowego Funduszu Walutowego: osiemdziesi\u0105t pi\u0119\u0107 miliard\xF3w euro. W radiu co drugie s\u0142owo to \"bailout\"."
    - speakerId: narrator
      language: 0
      text: "Restauracja Declana przetrwa\u0142a. Kr\xF3tsze menu, ta\u0144sze wino, ten sam zlew. Kuba prowadzi kuchni\u0119 od otwarcia do zamkni\u0119cia."
    - speakerId: declan
      language: 1
      text: Sixty-two, Kooba. My knees are older than this country's debt. Will you take the kitchen? Properly. Your name on the door.
    - speakerId: kuba_thought
      language: 0
      text: "Moje nazwisko na drzwiach. \"Kooba\", przez dwa \"o\", jak na pierwszej kopercie z wyp\u0142at\u0105."
    teachVocabularyWords: []
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags: []
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: 0
      homesickness: 0
      integration: 0
    choices:
    - choiceText: "Bior\u0119. Z twoim nazwiskiem obok."
      targetNodeId: wh_take
      requiredFlag: 
    - choiceText: Jeszcze nie. Daj mi rok.
      targetNodeId: wh_year
      requiredFlag: 
    branchIfFlag: 
    branchNodeId: 
    nextNodeId: 
  - nodeId: wh_take
    lines:
    - speakerId: declan
      language: 1
      text: Two names on the door. Grand. Mine first, though. For now.
    - speakerId: kuba_thought
      language: 0
      text: "Ka\u017Cdy kiedy\u015B od tego zaczyna\u0142. Ja zacz\u0105\u0142em od dwudziestu euro i zlewu."
    teachVocabularyWords: []
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags:
    - ch6_name_on_the_door
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: 0
      homesickness: 0
      integration: 10
    choices: []
    branchIfFlag: 
    branchNodeId: 
    nextNodeId: 
  - nodeId: wh_year
    lines:
    - speakerId: declan
      language: 1
      text: A year. You're the only man in this country asking for more time instead of more money.
    - speakerId: kuba_thought
      language: 0
      text: "Czas to jedyna rzecz, kt\xF3rej banki jeszcze nie zagwarantowa\u0142y."
    teachVocabularyWords: []
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags:
    - ch6_asked_for_a_year
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: 0
      homesickness: 0
      integration: 0
    choices: []
    branchIfFlag: 
    branchNodeId: 
    nextNodeId: 
  - nodeId: wh_perth
    lines:
    - speakerId: narrator
      language: 0
      text: "29 listopada 2010. Pilbara, Australia Zachodnia. Ob\xF3z g\xF3rniczy na czterysta os\xF3b, czterdzie\u015Bci stopni w cieniu, kt\xF3rego nie ma."
    - speakerId: narrator
      language: 0
      text: "Kuba i Gavin prowadz\u0105 kuchni\u0119: trzy zmiany, tysi\u0105c dwie\u015Bcie posi\u0142k\xF3w dziennie, pensja, o jakiej w Dublinie nikomu si\u0119 nie \u015Bni\u0142o."
    - speakerId: gavin
      language: 1
      text: Kooba. It's forty degrees and I'd give a week's wages for one day of Dublin rain. Is that mad?
    - speakerId: kuba_thought
      language: 0
      text: "Gavin t\u0119skni za deszczem. Ja t\u0119skni\u0119... nie wiem ju\u017C, za kt\xF3rym miejscem. Chyba za kuchni\u0105, w kt\xF3rej wszyscy znali moje imi\u0119."
    teachVocabularyWords: []
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags: []
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: 0
      homesickness: 0
      integration: 0
    choices:
    - choiceText: "M\xF3wi\u0119 mu, \u017Ce to normalne. Ja t\u0119skni\u0119 za dwoma krajami naraz."
      targetNodeId: wh_two
      requiredFlag: 
    - choiceText: "Proponuj\u0119, \u017Ceby\u015Bmy na \u015Bwi\u0119ta polecieli do Dublina."
      targetNodeId: wh_christmas
      requiredFlag: 
    branchIfFlag: 
    branchNodeId: 
    nextNodeId: 
  - nodeId: wh_two
    lines:
    - speakerId: gavin
      language: 1
      text: Two countries. Jaysus. You're richer than me, so.
    teachVocabularyWords: []
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags:
    - ch6_two_homes
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: 0
      homesickness: -5
      integration: 5
    choices: []
    branchIfFlag: 
    branchNodeId: 
    nextNodeId: 
  - nodeId: wh_christmas
    lines:
    - speakerId: gavin
      language: 1
      text: Dublin for Christmas... Declan would cry. Then he'd put us to work.
    teachVocabularyWords: []
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags:
    - ch6_christmas_in_dublin
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: 0
      homesickness: -5
      integration: 0
    choices: []
    branchIfFlag: 
    branchNodeId: 
    nextNodeId: 
  - nodeId: wh_poland
    lines:
    - speakerId: narrator
      language: 0
      text: "29 listopada 2010. Krak\xF3w. Na Rynku rozstawiaj\u0105 jarmark bo\u017Conarodzeniowy, a w hotelowej kuchni przy Rynku od sz\xF3stej rano pachnie barszczem i roso\u0142em."
    teachVocabularyWords: []
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags: []
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: 0
      homesickness: 0
      integration: 0
    choices: []
    branchIfFlag: ch5_krakow_job
    branchNodeId: wh_sous
    nextNodeId: wh_climbed
  - nodeId: wh_sous
    lines:
    - speakerId: narrator
      language: 0
      text: "Kuba jest tu zast\u0119pc\u0105 szefa kuchni od dw\xF3ch lat. Certyfikat z Cathal Brugha Street wisi w biurze szefa, obok menu na Euro 2012."
    - speakerId: kuba_thought
      language: 0
      text: "W Dublinie by\u0142em \"Kooba\". Tu jestem \"panem Jakubem\". Nie wiem, kt\xF3ry z nich lepiej kroi cebul\u0119."
    teachVocabularyWords: []
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags: []
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: 0
      homesickness: 0
      integration: 0
    choices: []
    branchIfFlag: 
    branchNodeId: 
    nextNodeId: wh_mum
  - nodeId: wh_climbed
    lines:
    - speakerId: narrator
      language: 0
      text: "Kuba zaczyna\u0142 tu od zlewu, jak w Dublinie. Po roku dosta\u0142 desk\u0119, po drugim ca\u0142\u0105 zmian\u0119. Szef kuchni m\xF3wi na niego \"Irlandczyk\"."
    - speakerId: kuba_thought
      language: 0
      text: "W Dublinie by\u0142em Polakiem. W Krakowie jestem Irlandczykiem. Wsz\u0119dzie troch\u0119 st\u0105d i troch\u0119 z daleka."
    teachVocabularyWords: []
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags: []
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: 0
      homesickness: 0
      integration: 0
    choices: []
    branchIfFlag: 
    branchNodeId: 
    nextNodeId: wh_mum
  - nodeId: wh_mum
    lines:
    - speakerId: mum
      language: 0
      text: "Kubu\u015B, przyjedziesz na Wigili\u0119? Tata ju\u017C kupi\u0142 karpia. \u017Bywego. P\u0142ywa w wannie i ma na imi\u0119 Declan."
    teachVocabularyWords: []
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags: []
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: 0
      homesickness: 0
      integration: 0
    choices:
    - choiceText: "Przyje\u017Cd\u017Cam. I zrobi\u0119 pierogi jak w Dublinie."
      targetNodeId: wh_wigilia
      requiredFlag: 
    - choiceText: "Mamo, w Wigili\u0119 hotel jest pe\u0142ny. Przyjad\u0119 w drugi dzie\u0144 \u015Bwi\u0105t."
      targetNodeId: wh_later
      requiredFlag: 
    branchIfFlag: 
    branchNodeId: 
    nextNodeId: 
  - nodeId: wh_wigilia
    lines:
    - speakerId: kuba_thought
      language: 0
      text: "Karp o imieniu Declan. Tata ma poczucie humoru, kt\xF3rego nikt w rodzinie nie podejrzewa\u0142."
    teachVocabularyWords: []
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags:
    - ch6_christmas_eve_home
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: 0
      homesickness: -10
      integration: 0
    choices: []
    branchIfFlag: 
    branchNodeId: 
    nextNodeId: 
  - nodeId: wh_later
    lines:
    - speakerId: mum
      language: 0
      text: No trudno. Karp poczeka. Declan jest cierpliwy.
    teachVocabularyWords: []
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags: []
    outcome:
